<p><a href="/alcohol-recommendations/#bourbon">Bourbon</a> is a type of Whiskey. It was created in America and is a barrel-aged distilled liquor that’s made primarily from corn.</p>
<p>The name Bourbon originates from the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Bourbon" rel="noopener">French Bourbon Dynasty,</a> but how this type of American whiskey got that name is up for debate.</p>
<p>Major contenders include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Bourbon Street in New Orleans</li>
<li>Bourbon County in Kentucky</li>
</ul>
<p>…with the latter the reason why Bourbon is so closely connected to Kentucky.</p>
<p>Interestingly, by law, <a href="/alcohol-recommendations/#bourbon">Bourbon</a> sold in the US must be produced in the US, be made from at least 51% corn, and stored in a container of charred oak.</p>
